{
  "_readme": [
    "Where wild crops and fruit trees generate. Applied at world load by kubejs/server_scripts/worldgen/wild_crops.js",
    "(CEConfig [worldgen.systems] wildCrops). Rejoin the world after editing; only chunks generated afterwards change.",
    "Reference + tests: feature_writeup/crops.md section 2.8. Resolved biome lists: feature_writeup/crops_by_biome.md",
    "(python3 tools/gen_crop_worldgen_table.py).",
    "",
    "biomes: every overworld biome -> its traits, space separated. Biomes marked 'ocean' or 'cave' never match a rule:",
    "  the crop features are placed at the surface, which is water or another biome there.",
    "  climate: cold | temperate | warm.  moisture: wet | dry (neither = moderate).  snowy.",
    "  ground: grassy sandy terracotta gravelly rocky icy muddy mycelium.",
    "  shape: forest plains mountain peak beach cliff coastal river swamp jungle desert badlands savanna shrubland",
    "         oasis mushroom sky.  trees: oak birch dark_oak coniferous cherry.  other: flower autumn.",
    "  A biome missing from this list (new mod) is reported by the generator and by wild_crops.js; it gets no crops.",
    "",
    "crops: one entry per biome list.",
    "  where: clauses, OR'ed. A clause is traits that must all hold; '!trait' must not hold.",
    "  add / except: biome ids added after / removed after the clauses.",
    "  features: placed features added to those biomes (via the biome tag creativeengineering:wild_crops/<key>).",
    "  disable_modifiers: the mods' own biome modifiers for this crop, replaced by forge:none.",
    "  remove_features: features that biome files list (vanilla patches via Terralith); removed from every overworld",
    "  biome, so 'features' must hold the pack's copy (creativeengineering:wild/*) instead.",
    "  label: shown in the reports.  notes: why, for the reader."
  ],

